nit, optional: `paneViews()` now means two things. On the base `PrimitiveWrapper` it's every view, which `Series` filters itself. On `PanePrimitiveWrapper` it's only the normal layer. How about renaming the base method to `allPaneViews()` with a single return type? Then `paneViews()` means "normal layer" for every source the pane draws, and the cast and `override` go away:

```ts
// PrimitiveWrapper
public allPaneViews(): readonly PrimitivePaneViewWrapper[] { /* body unchanged */ }

// PanePrimitiveWrapper
private _paneViewsByZOrder(zOrder: PrimitivePaneViewZOrder): readonly PrimitivePaneViewWrapper[] {
	return this.allPaneViews().filter((view: PrimitivePaneViewWrapper) => view.zOrder() === zOrder);
}
```

Its only other caller is `primitivePaneViewsExtractor` in `src/model/series.ts`, which becomes `wrapper.allPaneViews()`. The comment above `paneViews()` can go as well. I tried this locally, and `tsc`, eslint and the unit tests pass.
